{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles and motion capabilities, with all possible uncontrollable sensor events and controllable motion actions. The specification automata E1 binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed, and ensuring rapid return to forward exploration. E2 prevents repeated recovery actions (oscillation), and E3 ensures full_rotate is only used as a last resort after repeated failures.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception/motion plant from decision/specification logic for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specification automata enforce safe, progress-maximizing action selection and restrict recovery/scan actions to appropriate contexts."
